{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/quickstart/index.html","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T02:27:30.516765Z","id":"6e8c06e5926c059ba971b3c0c2044a9c9a9101a6d61adc79b5305ba346f1d74f","body":{"detail":"tab-ideas (index.html:19) is shown when the page's extensions documents hold ideas (:577-582), and its links and the per-step ideas (:513) point at ideas.html. The seeded artifact holds only the release's clax.json, index.html and style.css, so the link 404s for a person who adds extensions docs to their copy. Fix by shipping ideas.html in the release or hiding the tab in a copy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":19},"end":{"line":19},"content_hash":"110cc16fde472f74d07b22b317999ebcc36c2200099f2eaee61d5731d61e196f"},"summary":"A seeded copy whose owner adds extensions docs shows a 'Make it better' tab linking to ideas.html, which a seeded copy does not ship","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/quickstart/index.html","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T18:52:22.666660Z","id":"85966025ab33d9e566cbe509c55744553cb0962c96ca8ac2e4d10e40b5ce3f23","body":{"detail":"HOSTED is true only when the shell's origin (SHELL, the first load's referrer kept in sessionStorage) is clax.dev or under it, because the sign-in step and its text name clax.dev. A person signed in on another hosted Clax (a self-hosted daemon in hosted mode) is never noticed, and ticks step 1 by hand. Deciding by 'not localhost, 127.0.0.1 or [::1]' would notice them, but would also tick a step titled 'Sign in to clax.dev' for a site that is not clax.dev, and a local daemon reached by a LAN address would pass.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":642},"end":{"line":647},"content_hash":"8a89ab32de63457dd14b984974dab554f178b0761a6048a1e2732c18c1ca9198"},"summary":"Treat any shell origin that is not loopback as hosted, rather than clax.dev alone","tags":["revisit:the quickstart's sign-in step names the site it runs on instead of clax.dev","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/quickstart/index.html","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T19:21:12.306509Z","id":"9ebecfab9028370702a0bfc153dd2d127c84a48ab90577aec0b58b763fa555ff","body":{"detail":"hosted() is true only when SHELL, the origin the shell capability's address() reports (web/shell/src/caps/shell.ts, the shell window's own location.origin), is clax.dev or under it, because the sign-in step and its text name clax.dev. The page cannot take the origin from document.referrer: the shell frames a site through /_clax/session/start, a 302 (crates/clax-server/src/routes/site.rs), and every site response carries Referrer-Policy: no-referrer (crates/clax-http/src/site_access.rs), so the referrer is always empty, and a page-chosen referrer would be spoofable besides. A person signed in on another hosted Clax (a self-hosted daemon in hosted mode) is never noticed, and ticks step 1 by hand. Deciding by 'not localhost, 127.0.0.1 or [::1]' would notice them, but would also tick a step titled 'Sign in to clax.dev' for a site that is not clax.dev, and a local daemon reached by a LAN address would pass.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":634},"end":{"line":639},"content_hash":"89d01188ea485b71effffb7d683cd954c2aa5f8c434996661f9caf0cf184ef73"},"summary":"Treat any shell origin that is not loopback as hosted, rather than clax.dev alone","supersedes":"85966025ab33d9e566cbe509c55744553cb0962c96ca8ac2e4d10e40b5ce3f23","tags":["revisit:the quickstart's sign-in step names the site it runs on instead of clax.dev","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/quickstart/index.html","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T19:39:53.718579Z","id":"f9fab8726fd59af43bd501dfaea37820dcf2854d5aed78cf3bc9a877f2018cc3","body":{"detail":"hosted() is true only when SHELL, the origin the shell capability's address() reports (web/shell/src/caps/shell.ts, the shell window's own location.origin), is clax.dev or under it, because the sign-in step and its text name clax.dev. The page cannot take the origin from document.referrer: the shell frames a site through the handshake page at /_clax/session/start, whose code /_clax/session redeems with a 302 (crates/clax-server/src/routes/site.rs), and every site response, that redirect included, carries Referrer-Policy: no-referrer (crates/clax-http/src/site_access.rs), so the referrer is always empty, and a page-chosen referrer would be spoofable besides. A person signed in on another hosted Clax (a self-hosted daemon in hosted mode) is never noticed, and ticks step 1 by hand. Deciding by 'not localhost, 127.0.0.1 or [::1]' would notice them, but would also tick a step titled 'Sign in to clax.dev' for a site that is not clax.dev, and a local daemon reached by a LAN address would pass.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":634},"end":{"line":639},"content_hash":"89d01188ea485b71effffb7d683cd954c2aa5f8c434996661f9caf0cf184ef73"},"summary":"Treat any shell origin that is not loopback as hosted, rather than clax.dev alone","supersedes":"9ebecfab9028370702a0bfc153dd2d127c84a48ab90577aec0b58b763fa555ff","tags":["revisit:the quickstart's sign-in step names the site it runs on instead of clax.dev","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/quickstart/index.html","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T22:31:33.497334Z","id":"f78ca1aff62f84d8f25b944603d575680d3653323527d974e53c0ccc6aa7f5d3","body":{"detail":"The figure shows only when reel.mp4 loads beside the page (web/quickstart/index.html, The reel). web/scripts/build-quickstart.mjs SHIPPED lists index.html, style.css, icon.svg, clax.json and logos/, so the copy seeded into each new clax.dev gallery has no video and the figure stays hidden there. The reel is a build artifact of web/reel kept out of the repository. Options: (a) upload it to the hosted quickstart's assets at release and point the page at that asset URL; (b) serve it from one fixed clax.dev path (a release asset the Worker serves) and give the video that src with reel.mp4 as the local fallback; (c) add it to the binary at build time from a release download (about 6 MB). Each needs the owner's call on where the reel lives.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":17},"end":{"line":21},"content_hash":"ed3cabe976f4981333c166cd9edf48469734a25ffc374854fc29296879097c0e"},"summary":"The seeded clax.dev quickstart never shows the reel: reel.mp4 is not among the shipped files","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/quickstart/index.html","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T23:45:59.056565Z","id":"a54073133d3087bac378c34c90ed53688833b536dfa4247b1b2e2f31510de356","body":{"detail":"The figure shows only when reel.mp4 loads beside the page (web/quickstart/index.html, The reel). web/scripts/build-quickstart.mjs SHIPPED lists index.html, style.css, icon.svg, clax.json and logos/, so the copy seeded into each new clax.dev gallery has no video and the figure stays hidden there. The reel is a build artifact of web/reel kept out of the repository. Options: (a) upload it to the hosted quickstart's assets at release and point the page at that asset URL; (b) serve it from one fixed clax.dev path (a release asset the Worker serves) and give the video that src with reel.mp4 as the local fallback; (c) add it to the binary at build time from a release download (about 6 MB). Each needs the owner's call on where the reel lives.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":12},"end":{"line":20},"content_hash":"0810fec5cec4de939e9ebae5395ac6e055bfdd26bb4f2ec3ff8a6755521e5dc4"},"summary":"The seeded clax.dev quickstart never shows the reel: reel.mp4 is not among the shipped files","supersedes":"f78ca1aff62f84d8f25b944603d575680d3653323527d974e53c0ccc6aa7f5d3","tags":["status:needs-decision","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/quickstart/index.html","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-27T23:45:59.137467Z","id":"feb974f6cf3a670a9529af5bce78f9e153e95f69ed0f1d8f4bfb4fe796c904ac","body":{"detail":"tab-ideas (index.html:23) is shown when the page's extensions documents hold ideas (:708-713), and its links and the per-step ideas (:602) point at ideas.html. The seeded artifact holds only the release's clax.json, index.html and style.css, so the link 404s for a person who adds extensions docs to their copy. Fix by shipping ideas.html in the release or hiding the tab in a copy.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":23},"end":{"line":23},"content_hash":"110cc16fde472f74d07b22b317999ebcc36c2200099f2eaee61d5731d61e196f"},"summary":"A seeded copy whose owner adds extensions docs shows a 'Make it better' tab linking to ideas.html, which a seeded copy does not ship","supersedes":"6e8c06e5926c059ba971b3c0c2044a9c9a9101a6d61adc79b5305ba346f1d74f","tags":["review","session:claude-code:e18aa7d7-bdd7-42c6-a52e-16a9153256f7"]}}
